          "text": "Skin lesion symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Rough itchy spots on hands and face. Multiple rough scaly spots had been mostly asymptomatic for months, with intermittent itch and irritation over the last few weeks, especially with gloves or a hat. No pain, bleeding, ulceration, or B symptoms reported."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Exposed skin examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Examination limited to face, scalp, neck, forearms, and hands. Fair skin (Fitzpatrick type II). Dozens of 2–6 mm erythematous, rough, scaly macules and papules on the dorsal hands, forearms, forehead, temples, and ears; sandpaper feel, non-tender, without induration, ulceration, or bleeding."
      }
    },
